<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Salatiga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-javanese-war-of-succession">Third Javanese War of Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Salatiga, signed in March 1757 in Salatiga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>, ended the long rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangkunegara-i">Raden Mas Said</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and the courts of Surakarta and Yogyakarta. He received lands carved from Surakarta's territory and the title Mangkunegara I, founding the Mangkunegaran principality. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-giyanti">Treaty of Giyanti</a> of 1755 it completed the division of the Mataram realm.</p></div>
